---
// Who may do what to a domain, across the frontdoor, shared and domain accounts: the roles and
// policies a request passes on its way to a gateway, and the role a release acts through. Drawn
// with Starlight's colour variables so it follows the light and dark themes.
import Diagram from "./Diagram.astro";
---

<Diagram title="Who may act on a domain" minWidth={600} maxWidth={900}>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 900 830"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="domain-trust-title domain-trust-desc"
  >
    <title id="domain-trust-title">Who may act on a domain</title>
    <desc id="domain-trust-desc">
      A request: the frontdoor account's edge role signs each request with SigV4. The domain's API,
      in the domain account, uses IAM authorisation, and its resource policy admits the edge role
      alone. The API assumes its own invoke role, which only API Gateway may assume, and which
      invokes only the domain's live alias. The domain's function runs in the isolated subnets and
      the domain security group, as its execution role, with a permission boundary. It writes only
      its own log group. It may invoke any gateway in its environment at its live alias, and only
      through the network's lambda endpoint, whose policy allows that alias alone. A release: the
      shared account's release worker, shared-release-worker, assumes the domain's deploy role,
      which trusts it by a condition. The deploy role creates and updates only its domain's
      function, passes only its own execution role, and reads only its domain's bundles in the code
      bucket. It is denied every Lambda action on gateway functions, and any function outside the
      isolated subnets or the domain security group.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker
        id="domain-trust-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="head"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Frontdoor account -->
    <rect class="section" x="20" y="20" width="420" height="120" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="section-title" x="36" y="48">Frontdoor account</text>

    <rect class="box" x="80" y="62" width="300" height="58" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="230" y="86">Edge role</text>
    <text class="sub mono" x="230" y="106">frontdoor-&lt;environment&gt;-edge</text>

    <!-- Shared account -->
    <rect class="section" x="460" y="20" width="420" height="120" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="section-title" x="476" y="48">Shared account</text>

    <rect class="box" x="480" y="62" width="200" height="58" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="580" y="86">Release worker</text>
    <text class="sub mono" x="580" y="106">shared-release-worker</text>

    <rect class="box" x="700" y="62" width="160" height="58" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="780" y="86">Code bucket</text>
    <text class="sub" x="780" y="106">domains' bundles</text>

    <!-- Domain account -->
    <rect class="section" x="20" y="170" width="860" height="640" rx="10"></rect>
    <text class="section-title" x="36" y="198">Domain account</text>

    <rect class="box" x="60" y="230" width="340" height="70" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="230" y="254">The domain's API</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="274">IAM authorisation on every method</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="291">its resource policy admits the edge role alone</text>

    <rect class="box" x="60" y="340" width="340" height="70" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="230" y="364">The API's invoke role</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="384">only API Gateway may assume it</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="401">invokes only the domain's <tspan class="mono">live</tspan> alias</text>

    <rect class="subnet" x="40" y="440" width="380" height="150" rx="8"></rect>
    <text class="note" x="52" y="460">isolated subnets</text>
    <text class="note end" x="408" y="460"><tspan class="mono">domain</tspan> security group</text>

    <rect class="box accent" x="60" y="472" width="340" height="104" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="230" y="496">The domain's function</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="516">runs as its execution role</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="534">with a permission boundary</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="552">writes only its own log group</text>

    <rect class="box" x="60" y="630" width="340" height="60" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="230" y="654">The network's <tspan class="mono">lambda</tspan> endpoint</text>
    <text class="sub" x="230" y="674">allows <tspan class="mono">gateway-&lt;environment&gt;-*:live</tspan> alone</text>

    <rect class="box" x="60" y="730" width="340" height="58" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="230" y="754">A gateway</text>
    <text class="sub mono" x="230" y="774">gateway-&lt;environment&gt;-&lt;id&gt;:live</text>

    <rect class="box" x="480" y="230" width="380" height="232" rx="6"></rect>
    <text class="label" x="670" y="256">The domain's deploy role</text>
    <text class="sub mono" x="670" y="276">domain-&lt;environment&gt;-&lt;domain&gt;-deploy</text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="298">trusts the worker's role, by a condition</text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="316">creates and updates only its domain's function</text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="334">passes only its own execution role</text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="352">reads only its domain's bundles</text>
    <line class="rule" x1="500" y1="368" x2="840" y2="368"></line>
    <text class="label small" x="670" y="392">Denied, whatever else it is allowed</text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="412">every action on <tspan class="mono">gateway-&lt;environment&gt;-*</tspan></text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="430">a function outside the isolated subnets</text>
    <text class="sub" x="670" y="448">or the <tspan class="mono">domain</tspan> security group</text>

    <!-- A request -->
    <line class="flow" x1="230" y1="120" x2="230" y2="228"></line>
    <text class="sub start" x="240" y="160">signs with SigV4</text>
    <line class="flow" x1="230" y1="300" x2="230" y2="338"></line>
    <text class="sub start" x="240" y="324">assumes</text>
    <line class="flow" x1="230" y1="410" x2="230" y2="470"></line>
    <text class="sub start" x="240" y="430">invokes <tspan class="mono">live</tspan></text>
    <line class="flow" x1="230" y1="576" x2="230" y2="628"></line>
    <text class="sub start" x="240" y="612">invokes a gateway, only through the endpoint</text>
    <line class="flow" x1="230" y1="690" x2="230" y2="728"></line>

    <!-- A release -->
    <line class="flow" x1="580" y1="120" x2="580" y2="228"></line>
    <text class="sub start" x="590" y="160">assumes</text>
    <line class="flow" x1="800" y1="230" x2="800" y2="122"></line>
    <text class="sub end" x="792" y="200">reads</text>
    <polyline class="flow" points="600,462 600,524 402,524"></polyline>
    <text class="sub" x="510" y="514">creates, updates</text>
  </svg>
</Diagram>

<style>
  .flow {
    marker-end: url(#domain-trust-arrow);
  }
  .rule {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }
</style>
